<style>
  body {
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(134, 17, 237, 0.18), transparent 35%),
      radial-gradient(circle at bottom left, rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.1), transparent 30%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #120641 0%, #0c0332 100%);
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
</style>

<div class="min-h-screen px-5 py-12 md:py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl text-white">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      {gettext("Claper in PowerPoint")}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-white/70">
      {gettext(
        "Keep your presentation as your own PowerPoint file and let Claper put the questions, the answers and the joining code on its slides."
      )}
    </p>

    <%!-- The two files carry this server's own address already, which is the
    whole point of serving them from here: the alternative is telling people to
    edit four places in each file by hand. --%>
    <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
      <div
        :for={
          file <- [
            # The names are what Office shows in its add-in list, and they are
            # fixed English strings in the manifests. Translating them here would
            # name a thing that is not in the menu, and gettext had already
            # matched "Claper" to an existing German translation of the word.
            %{
              name: "Claper",
              what: gettext("The sidebar. Write polls and quizzes without leaving PowerPoint."),
              url: @sidebar_manifest_url,
              filename: "claper-sidebar.xml"
            },
            %{
              name: "Claper on a slide",
              what:
                gettext("The block you place on a slide. Shows one poll, quiz or the messages."),
              url: @slide_manifest_url,
              filename: "claper-on-a-slide.xml"
            }
          ]
        }
        x-data="{ copied: false }"
        class="rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5"
      >
        <p class="font-semibold">{file.name}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-white/60">{file.what}</p>

        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          <a href={file.url} download={file.filename} class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">
            {gettext("Download")}
          </a>
          <%!-- Says "copied" only once it was. navigator.clipboard does not
          exist outside a secure context, which a self-hosted Claper reached over
          plain http is, so the call is guarded rather than left to throw. Either
          way the address is printed below in full and can be selected by hand.
          The URL comes from this server's own configuration, and its quotes are
          escaped so it cannot end the string it sits in. --%>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-soft" x-on:click={copy_script(file.url)}>
            <span x-show="!copied">{gettext("Copy link")}</span>
            <span x-show="copied" x-cloak>{gettext("Copied")}</span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <%!-- Not fainter than this: measured against the painted ground, /40 at
        this size comes out at 3.7:1, and this is an address somebody may have to
        read off the screen and type somewhere else. --%>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-white/60 break-all">{file.url}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-lg font-semibold">{gettext("Two ways to install them")}</h2>

    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
      <%!-- The admin route is first because it is the one that scales: nobody
      shares a folder, and it reaches everyone at once. --%>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
        <p class="font-semibold">{gettext("Your administrator does it once")}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/60">
          {gettext(
            "In the Microsoft 365 admin center: Settings, Integrated apps, Upload custom apps. Paste one of the links above instead of a file, and choose who gets it. Repeat for the second one. It can take up to a day to appear."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
        <p class="font-semibold">{gettext("Or just for yourself")}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/60">
          {gettext(
            "Download both files into a folder and share that folder. In PowerPoint: File, Options, Trust Center, Trust Center Settings, Trusted Add-in Catalogs. Add the folder's network path, tick Show in Menu, restart. On a Mac put the files in the wef folder instead."
          )}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-white/60">
      {gettext("Both then appear under Insert, Add-ins, and the sidebar explains the rest.")}
    </p>

    <%!-- Said plainly rather than left to be discovered: the sidebar key is the
    one thing here that must not travel, and this page is public. --%>
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-5">
      <p class="text-sm text-white/60">
        {gettext(
          "The sidebar asks for a key when you first open it. You create that in your event's settings, it can create and delete questions, and it belongs on your own computer rather than inside a presentation you send around."
        )}
      </p>
      <a href={~p"/events"} class="btn btn-sm btn-soft mt-4">{gettext("Go to my events")}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
